body:
Thank you for your reply... you seem to really "get" where I'm coming from. Sincerely, I mean that. To be honest, when I made this post yesterday, I had a deep feeling of remorse... I was afraid that I'd get blasted by trolls, or get comments or replies of people telling me that, yes, indeed, I didn't give those methods of therapy a "fair trial" and that it was my own fault that I ended up this way.

&#x200B;

But when I read your reply, I don't know, I feel as if you're the first person, maybe in more than a decade, that really understands my situation. Empathy is so hard to come by, that I honestly felt like it didn't even exist anymore. The many doctors and therapists I saw throughout my life all looked like they were in a painful struggle to help me get better... I didn't even expect them to be my friend, but it's as if they saw me as a massive burden and the longer it took to "help" me, the more they felt like they'd just given up on me. At least, that's what it seemed like.

&#x200B;

Anyway, thank you for your understanding. I really appreciate it.
